## Installation

> Installation instructions will be added as the first usable release is published.

For development:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/LALSINGH16-code/OpenJarvis.git

cd OpenJarvis

python -m venv .venv
```

### Linux

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate
```

### Windows

```powershell
.venv\Scripts\activate
```

Install dependencies:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

Run:

```bash
python -m openjarvis
```

---

## AI Providers

### OpenRouter

OpenRouter provides access to many AI models through a single API.

You can configure an OpenRouter API key and select the model you want to use.

### Ollama

Ollama allows OpenJarvis to connect to models running locally on your computer.

This provides an option for users who want to keep AI processing local.

### Direct Providers

OpenJarvis is designed to support direct integrations with providers such as:

* OpenAI
* Google Gemini
* Anthropic
* Groq

More providers can be added through the provider architecture.

---

## Configuration

API keys should never be committed to GitHub.

Use environment variables or the OpenJarvis configuration system.

Example:

```env
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=
```

Keep your `.env` file private.

---

## Security

OpenJarvis can interact with your operating system.

That means security is a major part of the project.

Potentially dangerous operations should require confirmation.

Examples include:

```text
Delete files
Shutdown computer
Restart computer
Kill processes
Execute destructive shell commands
Modify sensitive system files
```

Never run AI-generated shell commands blindly.

---

## Plugins

OpenJarvis is designed to support plugins.

Future plugins may provide capabilities such as:

```text
Weather
Spotify
GitHub
Email
Calendar
Web search
YouTube
Smart home
Developer tools
```

The plugin system will allow developers to extend OpenJarvis without modifying the core assistant.

